  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $7+42+252+\\,\u22ef?$ Express your answer as a function of $N.$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{42}{7} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=7$ and $r=6.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{7(1-{6}^{N})}{1-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{7(1-{6}^{N})}{(-5)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{5}(1-{6}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}({6}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
